	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;    This actually fetches the user&apos;s LDAP roles, when using the LdapRealm, so they&apos;re accessible on Zeppelin (via the `SecurityUtils`).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    As I debugged through it, I found some weird replacement code, so I wrote some tests around the `LdapRealm` and fixed what I believe was wrong there. Eg.: `expandTemplate` would expand, for instance, `uid=&lt;/p&gt;
{0}` into `uid={0}
&lt;p&gt;yourusername`.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    In order to make the actual LDAP calls for roles, I exposed the `queryForAuthorizationInfo` method and used it on `SecurityUtils`. &lt;/p&gt;

